# Copy to .dev.vars (git-ignored). Used by `wrangler dev` and, as a fallback, by `npm run eval`.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# Only `npm run eval` with a gemini-* model reads this; the Worker never does. Create it in Google AI Studio on a
# project with billing enabled. Google's free-tier terms have let it use what is sent to improve its products (check
# the current terms on ai.google.dev before relying on either tier), and in production these would be users' pages.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=...
# Shared secret the app sends as x-app-key. Any long random string.
APP_KEY=change-me-to-a-long-random-string
# Only for testing a purchase made through Xcode's local StoreKit configuration. Those transactions are
# signed by a certificate Xcode generates on this machine (CN=StoreKit Testing in Xcode, about a year's
# validity), which is its own leaf and root at once — a one-certificate chain. Pin it here or nothing
# bought in the simulator will verify. Leave it unset to pin Apple's root, which is what production does;
# the two are mutually exclusive, and setting this also accepts `environment: "Xcode"`.
#
# Export it: open ios/RecipeBasket.storekit in Xcode, then Editor > Save Public Certificate, then
#   openssl x509 -in ~/Downloads/StoreKitTestCertificate.cer -inform der -noout -fingerprint -sha256
# It is NOT the StoreKitTestCertificate.cer inside the Xcode bundle — that one signs nothing. The value
# changes when Xcode regenerates the certificate, so a verification that suddenly fails with
# `entitlementRejected: "signature"` usually means it needs exporting again.
# XCODE_ROOT_FINGERPRINT=F4:6E:BA:...
